10→The fundamental problem is the LLM is merging \"Prospero\" with \"the mummer\" instead of with \"Prince Prospero\".\n   111→\n   112→**Option A: Pre-merge heuristic rule**\n   113→Add a rule BEFORE pairwise decisions:\n   114→- If name A is a substring of name B (e.g., \"Prospero\" in \"Prince Prospero\"), prefer merging A with B\n   115→- \"Prospero\" should merge with \"Prince Prospero\" (substring match) NOT \"the mummer\" (no name overlap)\n   116→\n   117→Location: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` - add pre-merge grouping\n   118→\n   119→**Option B: Epithet vs proper name distinction**\n   120→\"the mummer\" starts with \"the\" (epithet/descriptor pattern)\n   121→\"Prospero\" is a proper name without article\n   122→These should NOT be merged by default without strong evidence\n   123→\n   124→Location: Add classification in proposer or validation stages\n   125→\n   126→### Priority 2: Add logging to death evidence split\n   127→\n   128→Add detailed logging to `_split_on_death_evidence()` to understand why it's not triggering:\n   129→- Log all mention contexts being scanned\n   130→- Log pattern matches found\n   131→- Log why split wasn't performed\n   132→\n   133→### Priority 3: Full-text death scanning (backup)\n   134→\n   135→If mention contexts don't contain death evidence, scan the FULL TEXT:\n   136→- Load the original text\n   137→- Find death patterns\n   138→- Extract character names from death scenes\n   139→- Force split if death relationship found\n   140→\n   141→### What NOT to Try Again\n   142→- Context window adjustments alone (attempts 7-15 proved insufficient)\n   143→- Prompt-based rules (attempts 3, 14 ineffective)\n   144→- Post-processing without fixing the root merge decision\n   145→\n   146→## Fix History\n   147→\n   148→### Attempts 1-15\n   149→See previous EVALUATION_STATE.md entries and git history.\n   150→\n   151→### Attempt 16\n   152→- **Change:** POST-PROCESSING character split based on death evide