ic_spelling\": null,\n  1379→      \"audio_url\": null,\n  1380→      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n  1381→      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: vegetables (PROH-doos); to make (pruh-DOOS)\"\n  1382→    },\n  1383→    {\n  1384→      \"word\": \"deliberate\",\n  1385→      \"flag_reason\": \"homograph\",\n  1386→      \"occurrences\": 1,\n  1387→      \"first_position\": 11611,\n  1388→      \"chapter_indices\": [\n  1389→        1\n  1390→      ],\n  1391→      \"context_examples\": [\n  1392→        \"...his group in the direction of the intruder, who, at the moment was also near at hand, and now, with deliberate and stately step, made closer approach to the speaker. But from a certain nameless awe with which t...\"\n  1393→      ],\n  1394→      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  1395→      \"ipa\": null,\n  1396→      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n  1397→      \"audio_url\": null,\n  1398→      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n  1399→      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: adj (di-LIB-er-it); verb (di-LIB-er-ayt)\"\n  1400→    }\n  1401→  ],\n  1402→  \"glossary\": null,\n  1403→  \"overview\": {\n  1404→    \"structure\": {\n  1405→      \"chapter_count\": 1,\n  1406→      \"has_titles\": false,\n  1407→      \"has_parts\": false,\n  1408→      \"narrative_style\": \"unknown\",\n  1409→      \"description\": \"This book contains 1 chapters. Chapters are numbered sequentially.\"\n  1410→    },\n  1411→    \"plot_summary\": {\n  1412→      \"plot_summary\": \"The story begins in the grip of a merciless plague known as the Red Death, a disease that spreads rapidly through society, marked by bleeding pores and fatal scarlet stains. As the world outside crumbles into fear and isolation, Prince Prospero, a man of extravagant tastes and defiant spirit, retreats with a thousand courtiers into the fortified walls of his abbey-like castle. There, he constructs a world of opulence and distraction—endless feasts, music, and revelry—attempting to escape the grim reality beyond. The castle, sealed from the outside world, becomes a sanctuary of indulgence, yet its very isolation underscores the futility of denying death’s inevitability. The prince, a figure of authority and excess, is surrounded by loyal nobles and courtiers who, though sheltered, remain unaware of the growing dread beneath the surface of their festivities.\\n\\nAs the fifth month of seclusion draws to a close, Prince Prospero hosts a grand masked ball in the seven uniquely decorated rooms of his castle, each adorned with stained-glass windows that reflect their respective colors—blue, purple, green, orange, white, violet, and finally, black. The final chamber, shrouded in darkness and lit by blood-red panes, houses a massive ebony clock that chimes each hour, halting all revelry and plunging the guests into silence and unease. The atmosphere grows increasingly tense with each chime, a reminder of time’s relentless march. Then, at midnight, a mysterious figure appears—dressed as the Red Death itself, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask. The guests are paralyzed with terror, unable to move or speak, as the figure moves through the rooms with eerie calm, symbolizing the inescapable presence of death.\\n\\nEnraged by the intrusion and the violation of his sanctuary, Prince Prospero draws a dagger and pursues the figure through all seven rooms, driven by a mix of fury and denial. His chase is a desperate attempt to reclaim control, to prove that even death can be defied. Yet, when he finally confronts the figure in the black chamber, he collapses dead—revealing the truth that the masked figure was not a man, but a manifestation of the plague itself. The revelation is immediate and absolute: the Red Death had infiltrated the castle long before, hidden among the revelers, and had claimed every life. As the clock chimes one final time, the lights go out, and darkness consumes the entire castle, leaving no survivors. The story ends with the complete annihilation of the illusion of safety, underscoring the futility of human attempts to evade fate.\",\n  1413→      \"themes\": [\n  1414→        \"identity\",\n  1415→        \"ambition\",\n  1416→        \"loss\"\n  1417→      ],\n  1418→      \"narrative_style\": \"first-person retrospective\"\n  1419→    },\n  1420→    \"model_usage\": {\n  1421→      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n  1422→        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n  1423→        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n  1424→      },\n  1425→      \"Character Extraction\": {\n  1426→        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n  1427→        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n  1428→      },\n  1429→      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n  1430→        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n  1431→        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n  1432→      },\n  1433→      \"Character Profiles\": {\n  1434→        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n  1435→        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n  1436→      },\n  1437→      \"Pronunciation Guide\": {\n  1438→        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n  1439→        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n  1440→      }\n  1441→    },\n  1442→    \"timing\": {\n  1443→      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n  1444→        \"duration_seconds\": 19.64,\n  1445→        \"duration_formatted\": \"19.6s\"\n  1446→      },\n  1447→      \"Character Extraction\": {\n  1448→        \"duration_seconds\": 314.88,\n  1449→        \"duration_formatted\": \"5m 15s\"\n  1450→      },\n  1451→      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n  1452→        \"duration_seconds\": 23.86,\n  1453→        \"duration_formatted\": \"23.9s\"\n  1454→      },\n  1455→      \"Character Profiles\": {\n  1456→        \"duration_seconds\": 0.01,\n  1457→        \"duration_formatted\": \"0.0s\"\n  1458→      },\n  1459→      \"Pronunciation Guide\": {\n  1460→        \"duration_seconds\": 91.2,\n  1461→        \"duration_formatted\": \"1m 31s\"\n  1462→      },\n  1463→      \"total\": {\n  1464→        \"duration_seconds\": 483.66,\n  1465→        \"du