h,' a fatal plague marked by bleeding pores and scarlet stains that isolates victims from society. Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his sealed, abbey-like castle, where he provides endless entertainment and indulgence to ignore the horrors outside. As the fifth month of seclusion ends, he hosts a lavish masked ball in seven uniquely colored rooms, each with stained-glass windows matching their hue, culminating in a black chamber with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting the festivities and instilling dread. During the midnight chime, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, causing terror and paralysis among the guests. Prince Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting it in the black chamber—revealing the figure to be empty, as the plague has infiltrated even their sanctuary, claiming every life as the lights extinguish and darkness claims all.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"characters\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\\\",\\n      \\\"canonical_name\\\": \\\"the Prince Prospero\\\",\\n      \\\"aliases\\\": [],\\n      \\\"role\\\": null,\\n      \\\"appearance\\\": null,\\n      \\\"personality\\\": null,\\n      \\\"voice_guidance\\\": null,\\n      \\\"descriptions\\\": [],\\n      \\\"relationships\\\": {},\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": [],\\n      \\\"voice_notes\\\": null,\\n      \\\"first_appearance_chapter\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"mention_count\\\": 3,\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"is_narrator\\\": false,\\n      \\\"narrative_role\\\": null\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"425644eb-8f8c-4772-bc09-33529767a9ca\\\",\\n      \\\"canonical_name\\\": \\\"the mummer\\\",\\n      \\\"aliases\\\": [\\n        \\\"Prospero\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"role\\\": null,\\n      \\\"appearan